credit cards have always seemed to be an anomoly since they don't do
the obvious. with keys and lock picks abounding, credit cards ought to
be given a more appropriate meaning ... tourists would naturally start
the game with a real credit card. some features surrounding a possible
credit implementation:

you "a"pply a credit card.
in what direction? [hjklyubn.]

if the adjacent object in the indicated direction is a door then you
    could unlock it, if appropriate.
if the adjacent object in the indicated direction is a shopkeeper
    in a shop then you could go into debt if you're not already in debt
    and purchase certain unpaid items that you choose from your inventory.
if the indicated direction is "." (i.e. yourself) you could use your
    charge card to restore expended charges in appropriate magic. this
    would involve the destruction of the card, as well. there's a chance
    that the card would not work as reliably as a scroll of charging.

there are some features associated with debt:
you cannot go further into debt if you are already in debt, the
    transaction would be refused.
you cannot buy other things at this or any other shop until you get out
    of debt. you can look and, of course, you could steal.
credit involves some overhead so your debt is greater than the amount you
    purchased. how, where and when to repay are explained to you before
    you go into debt and you must agree to those terms or the transaction
    is refused. the "p"ay command is used to repay.
if your debt was $100 gold pieces you would have to repay $150 gold pieces
    at the original shop to get out of debt. optionally you would have to
    pay $200 gold pieces at any other shop (or temple!) to get out of
    debt. you don't have to repay in full at any one time but you must
    be repaid in full on time to avoid the human, @, "repo-man".
when you enter debt you can enjoy 2000 moves without consequence. while
    in debt your score is lowered by the amount of your debt. when you
    are out of debt you score would be "accurate" again.
while in debt every 500 moves you would be given a message or
    feeling about your debt status, perhaps like:
    [ 500] you feel like someone is checking your credit history.
    [1000] you feel like your account is overdrawn.
    [1500] you feel like you are living on borrowed time.
    [2000] you feel like someone is after you for your money.
if you do not repay your debt in the alloted time then for every 1000
    gold pieces you owe, an angry "repo-man" is generated that will seek
    you wherever you go! the "repo-man", @, is not out to kill you, his
    attack would do minor damage, however his magic attack would be like
    a nymphs but not as charming. your repossessed items are carried by
    the "repo-man" for awhile, however at times the repossessed items
    carried by the "repo-man" are  magically delivered back to the original
    shop. you could repay the "repo-man" at the 2x rate.
when your debt is cleared the "repo-man" becomes peaceful and doesn't
    attack. if you kill a "repo-man" the Keystone Kops are alerted and
    you would lose telepathy.

why give credit?
if properly used it extends the players ability to acquire magic and
improves the chances for survival. abusing the credit system wouldn't
directly get you killed but would hamper your game. all suggestions
and comments are welcome ...
